# Change the order of the groups. Start the API with Aspire first, then send the first two requests once.
@host = http://localhost:5279

### Create an account → 201. The requests below use its access token.
# @name createAccount
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "user-{{$guid}}@example.com",
  "password": "password",
  "timeZone": "Europe/Zagreb"
}

### The groups → 200. A new account's groups can take a moment to appear.
# @name groups
GET {{host}}/api/v1/groups
Authorization: Bearer {{createAccount.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### A list that leaves out groups → 409 group.order_out_of_date.
PUT {{host}}/api/v1/group-order
Authorization: Bearer {{createAccount.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "groupIds": ["{{groups.response.body.$[1].id}}", "{{groups.response.body.$[0].id}}"]
}
